	<xs:complexType name="IdentityDocument">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="documentType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides information related to the type of legal document (e.g. PASSPORT).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:simpleType>
					<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
						<xs:enumeration value="CREW_MEMBER_CERTIFICATE"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="REDRESS"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="PASSPORT_CARD"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="VISA"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="KNOWN_TRAVELER"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="MILITARY_ID_CARD"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="RESIDENT_CARD"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="DRIVER_LICENCE"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="ALIEN_REGISTRATION"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="PASSPORT"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="IDENTITY_CARD"/>
						<xs:enumeration value="OTHER"/>
					</xs:restriction>
				</xs:simpleType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="number" type="xs:string">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the document number shown on the document. (e.g. QFU514563221J).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="issuanceDate" type="xs:date" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Date at which the document has been issued using format (e.g. 2017-02-01).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="expiryDate" type="xs:date" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Date after which the document is not valid any more using fromat (e.g. 2017-12-31).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="effectiveDate" type="xs:date" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Date at which the document starts to be valid using format (e.g. 2017-02-01).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="issuanceCountry" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the document issuance country code using ISO 3166-1 standard (e.g. FR for France)</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:simpleType>
					<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
						<xs:length value="2"/>
					</xs:restriction>
				</xs:simpleType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="issuanceLocation" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A more precise information concerning the place where the document has been issued such as state, department or a city name (e.g. New-York).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="name" type="PersonName" minOccurs="0"/>
			<xs:element name="gender" type="Gender" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Gender information.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="nationality" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides information related to nationalities using ISO 3166-1 standard (e.g. “LV”).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="birthDate" type="xs:date" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the birth date using format (e.g. 2000-10-20)</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="birthPlace" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the birth place (e.g. Paris)</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="birthCountry" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the country of birth using ISO 3166-1 standard (e.g FR for France)</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
				<xs:simpleType>
					<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
						<xs:length value="2"/>
					</xs:restriction>
				</xs:simpleType>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="civilStatus" type="CivilStatus" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Civil status information.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="remarks" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="5">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Any kind of remarks including special conditions that can be found on the document</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="additionnalNames" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="10">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Used to convey the names of the people who can also use the document. For instance, the children of the document holder (e.g. Mathieu Henry).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="label" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Short description of the document.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="tags" type="Tag" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the category of the data elements to which this type makes reference</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="rank" type="xs:integer" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>In case several contact elements are provided, the rank indicates which element should be considered in priority. Rank "1" indicates the highest priority. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="sources" type="SourceReference" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="IdentityMetaData">
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="paxAssociationCount" type="xs:long" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>
          Description:
            Total number of pax associations for a PNR element in the same PNR.

          Example:
            Considering following PNR
--- RLR --- RP/NCE0Z01ME/NCE0Z01ME            MA/SU   8JAN19/1444Z   MQVCIM 1.KNG/TCHLL   2.PTR/PRKR   3.TN/STRK 4  0Z 300 Y 23MAY 4 POSCCS HK3          0700 0855   *1A/E* 5 AP NCE TBA - 0Z DUMMY AIRLINE IMPLEMENTATION - A 6 AP M654321/P1-2 7 AP M7654321/P3 8 AP M87654321 9 APE KNGTCHLL@BLCKPNTHR.COM/P1 10 APE PTRPRKR@SPDRMN.COM/P2 11 APE TNSTRK@RNMN.COM/P3 12 APE SUPERHEROESR@MRVL.COM 13 TK OK08JAN/NCE0Z01ME 14 FP CASH
Contact elements are associated to the different passengers of the PNR as below.
Contact PNR element    | Value                            | PassengerAssociation Details    | paxAssociationCount ---------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------- email                  | TNSTRK@RNMN.COM                  | P3                              | 1 email                  | SUPERHEROESR@MRVL.COM            | P1, P2, P3                      | 3 email                  | PTRPRKR@SPDRMN.COM               | P2                              | 1 email                  | KNGTCHLL@BLCKPNTHR.COM           | P1                              | 1 phone                  | 654321                           | P1, P2                          | 2 phone                  | 7654321                          | P3                              | 1 phone                  | 87654321                         | P1, P2, P3                      | 3
The paxAssociationCount is a data computed thanks PNR element associations.
          </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="IndividualBaggage">
